{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Raymond III Count of Tripoli also known as Raymond II of Toulouse was a nobleman born in 1140 in the County of Toulouse and died in 1187 in the County of Tripoli. He was the son of Alfonso Jordan Count of Toulouse and Faydith of Toulouse.\n\n### Early life and reign\n\nIn 1152 Raymond III married Hodierna of Jerusalem the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene. The marriage produced three children: Bohemond Count of Tripoli, Baldwin Count of Tripoli and a daughter named Melisende.\n\nRaymond III became Count of Tripoli in 1152 after his father's death. During his reign he faced numerous challenges including conflicts with the Assassins a Muslim sect and the Zengid Dynasty.\n\n### Crusades and conflicts\n\nRaymond III participated in the Second Crusade in 1148 and fought alongside King Louis VII of France and Conrad III of Germany. However, the crusade was unsuccessful and Raymond III returned to Tripoli.\n\nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din the Zengid ruler of Aleppo and Damascus. Raymond III remained a prisoner until 1173 when he was released in exchange for the release of several Muslim prisoners.\n\nAfter his release Raymond III resumed his reign in Tripoli and continued his conflicts with the Assassins and the Zengid Dynasty. He also supported the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where he was killed in action.\n\n### Legacy\n\nRaymond III's reign was marked by his conflicts with Muslim powers and his participation in the Crusades. He played a significant role in the defense of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\nRaymond III's legacy is remembered for his military prowess and his contributions to the Crusades. He is also remembered for his efforts to maintain the stability of the County of Tripoli during a time of conflict and upheaval.\n\nDespite the challenges he faced during his reign Raymond III left a lasting impact on the County of Tripoli and the Crusades. His military victories and political maneuvers helped to secure the county's borders and protect its interests.\n\nIn conclusion, Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a formidable leader who played a crucial role in the defense of the County of Tripoli and the Crusades. His legacy is remembered for his military prowess, political acumen, and contributions to the Crusades.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -3.9219088648678735e-05}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.0001627074379939586}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.3794739544391632}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -8.940656698541716e-06}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "also", "logprob": -0.515670657157898}, {"token": "known", "logprob": -0.0033385988790541887}, {"token": "as", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -1.549708758830093e-05}, {"token": "II", "logprob": -0.5765655040740967}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.00020776021119672805}, {"token": "T", "logprob": -0.8452842831611633}, {"token": "oul", "logprob": -0.0013308010529726744}, {"token": "ouse", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.003964660689234734}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.6054650545120239}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -1.3042383193969727}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.0143194030970335}, {"token": "born", "logprob": -0.8396637439727783}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.0006087357178330421}, {"token": "", "logprob": -0.1804913580417633}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.005352093372494e-05}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -7.629103492945433e-05}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.06833673268556595}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.4122387170791626}, {"token": "County", "logprob": -0.2049281746149063}, {"toke